    {
      "heading": "A new name near the gold line",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "wkdrbwnd1 reached 26th at 36.77 in the final observation before the Early cutoff. The recorded score transition was from 30.70, with the event showing a climb from 483rd. That leaves 1.21 points to the provisional public gold cutoff of 37.98. It is the morning’s sharpest late move near that boundary, without a change at the top.\n\ngoonew also made headway, adding 3.86 since the midnight comparison to reach 35.91 and close 38th. Its earlier score event put it 37th; the closing board moved it back one place. Those are two observations of the same advance, not two separate gains."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The strongholds hold",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-mark-barney-identity-0",
        "person-son-pham-identity-0",
        "person-keith-tyser-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs leads at 68.91, with Yi-Chia Chen second at 67.49. Their gap remains 1.42 points. Team Turducken is third at 52.82, ahead of mtg and the last dance. NVARC3 remains tenth at 43.94. All ten leading entries retain their places and scores against the midnight comparison.\n\nThe corrected illustration shows Team Turducken’s full seven-character crew: Mark, Son, Keith’s yellow mascot, DZ, NT, Choryu’s MRI-display character and Herminator standing in for Ronen, with two Yorkies. The flying machinery is editorial fantasy, not evidence of a new submission or the team’s equipment."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A fixed gold line, a moving field",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-19-2158-arc-3-ltzyc-surges-to-thirty-fifth",
        "wire-2026-10-19-2003-arc-3-arc-3-gold-line-slips"
      ],
      "text": "The wire’s earlier report put _LT_zyc at 35th after a rise to 36.00. That rolling-window report supplies context for the chase; it is not a fresh gain to add to this issue’s midnight totals. The same distinction applies to the wire’s earlier fall in the gold line: the closing gold cutoff is still 37.98, matching the midnight baseline.\n\npensukesan’s later recorded transition lifted its score from 29.97 to 34.99; it closes 47th. There is activity beneath the leaders even while the leading ten hold. Public medal positions remain provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Inside the Citadel, after the announcement",
      "sourceIds": [
        "dispatch-2026-10-19-tufa-two-racks-two-strongholds",
        "wire-2026-10-20-0400-arc-3-tufa-labs-racks-live-stockholm",
        "social-2112165331292602740"
      ],
      "text": "Last night’s commissioned Citadel feature examines Tufa’s announcement that two NVIDIA GB300 NVL72 racks are live in Stockholm, with DELTA handling installation and T.Loop hosting. The original public post still makes that claim. The full feature follows the deployment film and separates NVIDIA’s platform specifications from what Tufa has disclosed.\n\nThat is useful context for a lab leading both contests. It does not establish that the new installation produced either existing score, or that a rack is assigned to each contest. The hardware announcement and the unchanged closing leaderboard remain separate facts."
